  "notes": "{割|わり}と is an adverb meaning \"relatively\" or \"fairly,\" often implying something exceeded expectations.\n\nVARIATIONS:\n- {割|わり}と (standard)\n- {割|わり}に (similar, but also used as particle meaning \"considering\")\n- わりかし (casual variation)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {割|わり}と{簡単|かんたん} (relatively easy)\n- {割|わり}と{好|す}き (rather like)\n- {割|わり}と{早|はや}い (fairly early)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {割|わり}と vs. {比較的|ひかくてき}: {比較的|ひかくてき} is more formal and objective; {割|わり}と is more casual and subjective.\n- {割|わり}と vs. けっこう: Both mean \"fairly/rather,\" but けっこう can also mean \"quite a lot\" or be stronger. They're often interchangeable.\n- {割|わり}と vs. なかなか: なかなか has a nuance of \"surprisingly good\" or \"not easily.\"\n\nRegister: Casual to neutral. Common in everyday conversation.",
